    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1986, by its Section 3401(a)(1), requires the Commission to assess and collect fees and annual charges in any fiscal year in amounts equal to all of the costs incurred by the Commission in a fiscal year. For the purposes of recovering this payment, this Section establishes a FERC ACA Unit Charge to be applicable to all jurisdictional transportation quantities transported. These costs will continue to be recovered under its current rates with customers.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This balance represents the impact of U.S. Tax Reform as applied to businesses subject to rate-regulated accounting. The regulatory liability will be amortized over varying terms that approximate the expected reversal of the underlying deferred tax assets and liabilities that gave rise to the regulatory liability.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Effective April 1, 2025, the Respondent's retainage rate is 0.687% and has been adjusted for the prospective twelve months ending March 31, 2026.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Gas Used - heaters, regulators, controllers, and other miscellaneous equipment.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The volumes used to calculate the Annual Charge Adjustment are 13,207,333 Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Effective April 1, 2025, the Respondent's retainage rate is 0.687% and has been adjusted for the prospective twelve months ending March 31, 2026.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent uses Platt's Gas Daily Chicago City Gate as the basis for valuing gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent has a Commission approved Transportation Retainage Adjustment mechanism that tracks shipper supplied gas. The applicable excess or deficient balance is included in the next annual calculation to collect deficiencies or pass back excesses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Shares were issued without par value.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; The volumes used to calculate the Annual Charge Adjustment are 13,207,333 Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">See Notes to Financial Statements - Transactions with Related Parties for the basis of allocated expenses.</link:footnote>
